WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.679
(funky instrumental music)

00:00:03.679 --> 00:00:05.725
- I just feel that I'm a person

00:00:05.725 --> 00:00:07.021
that has something to say,

00:00:07.021 --> 00:00:09.558
and instead of saying it and using words,

00:00:09.558 --> 00:00:13.558
says it by just putting
some paint on a surface.

00:00:21.315 --> 00:00:25.482
My name is Halwani, and I'm
a street artist from Beirut.

00:00:26.661 --> 00:00:28.086
The reason I paint portraits

00:00:28.086 --> 00:00:32.085
or figures that kind of show
our country is very simple.

00:00:32.085 --> 00:00:33.997
When I started painting all over the city,

00:00:33.997 --> 00:00:36.181
I used to have to remove
photos of politicians,

00:00:36.181 --> 00:00:39.552
and political logos and election posters.

00:00:39.552 --> 00:00:42.200
These politicians weren't
necessarily good at their job,

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.125
occupy most of the urban landscape,

00:00:44.125 --> 00:00:46.472
and this is where I actually
wanted to replace them

00:00:46.472 --> 00:00:49.506
with something more positive
that the citizens of Beirut,

00:00:49.506 --> 00:00:53.673
that the presence of these
people is really optional.

00:00:59.824 --> 00:01:02.794
There's a very complicated
question of identity,

00:01:02.794 --> 00:01:06.512
when it comes to: what does
it mean to be Lebanese?

00:01:06.512 --> 00:01:08.602
And this is another reason
why I paint these faces.

00:01:08.602 --> 00:01:11.307
They represent the stories
of Lebanon, Beirut,

00:01:11.307 --> 00:01:14.085
and the Arab world in general.

00:01:14.085 --> 00:01:15.925
A mural can make a wall not only a wall,

00:01:15.925 --> 00:01:19.070
but maybe something that creates

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:22.880
a relationship of people with
an element in the street,

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:25.153
and I think it kind of spreads positivity

00:01:25.153 --> 00:01:27.133
and changes the perspective of people

00:01:27.133 --> 00:01:29.216
from their everyday life.

00:01:30.793 --> 00:01:34.593
I really appreciate the people
that compare me to Banksy.

00:01:34.593 --> 00:01:36.044
I really appreciate Banksy's work,

00:01:36.044 --> 00:01:38.558
and I think it's smart, it’s, uh, witty,

00:01:38.558 --> 00:01:40.324
and he has a lot of credit

00:01:40.324 --> 00:01:44.324
when it comes to the
global street art movement.

00:01:47.187 --> 00:01:49.590
I don't paint just for
the sake of painting,

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:52.531
or for the sake of capitalizing
on a certain event.

00:01:52.531 --> 00:01:53.640
I just paint when I feel

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:57.140
that I have something constructive to say.

